   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the vehicle and traffic law and the state finance law, in relation to a mandatory surcharge for traffic offenses and infractions in Suffolk and Nassau counties",
    "basePrintNo": "S6018",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6018-2009",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §1809-f, V & T L; add §97-jjjj, St Fin L",
    "lawSection": "Vehicle and Traffic Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S6018\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act to amend the vehicle and traffic law and the state finance law,\nin relation to a mandatory surcharge for traffic offenses and\ninfractions in Suffolk and Nassau counties\n\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nThis bill would impose a mandatory fifty dollar surcharge on certain\ntraffic convictions adjudicated in the Suffolk County or Nassau County\nPolice Districts.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1 of the bill adds vehicle and traffic law (\"VTL\") § 1909-f\nwhich would require that convictions of traffic infractions\nadjudicated in Nassau and Suffolk are to be levied a surcharge of\nfifty dollars. The surcharge will be deposited in the Long Island\nExpressway and Sunrise Highway Patrol Fund.\n\nSection 2 of the bill adds VTL § 97-jjjj to establish the Long Island\nExpressway and Sunrise Highway Patrol Fund. The funds are to be used\nexclusively to offset the costs of staffing the patrol units for the\nLong Island Expressway and the sunrise Highway in Suffolk and Nassau.\n\nSection 3 of the bill provides that it will be effective immediately.\n\n EXISTING LAW :\n\nVTL § 1809 establishes various mandatory surcharges.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNone.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nDue to the fact that the Long Island Expressway and Sunrise Highway do\nnot currently have a sufficient number of Suffolk County Police\nDepartment patrolling officers, this bill will help off-set the costs\nof properly staffing the patrol units for these state roads. Nassau\nand Suffolk Counties each spend approximately $12 million per year\npolicing their sections of the Long Island Expressway and Sunrise\nHighway. This legislation will substantially cover the law enforcement\nexpenses of Suffolk and Nassau counties by surcharging those who\nviolate the law.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone to the State.\n\nThis legislation would generate approximately $6.7 million in revenue\nfor Suffolk County and approximately $7.9 million in revenue for\nNassau County.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThe act takes effect immediately upon enactment.\n",
